    <string name="tag_separators_about">Tags like “Artist A/Artist B” are split into separate artists or composers on the delimiters you choose. Word delimiters such as “feat.” only match whole words, so “ft.” never splits “Daft Punk”. Genres use their own list, because names like “Hip-Hop/Rap” or “R&amp;B/Soul” contain “/” and “&amp;”. Put a backslash before a delimiter to keep it: “AC\\/DC” stays one artist. Changes apply the next time the library is scanned.</string>
